# Pulled Kaggle artifacts — what is committed, and why.
#
# COMMITTED (Arian works from this repo, and these are the report's content):
#   Grad-CAM / XAI figures, analysis CSV + JSON, kernel logs, probabilities.npy
#
# NOT COMMITTED — two exclusions, each for a concrete reason:
#
#   *.pth
#     GitHub HARD-REJECTS any file over 100 MB. weights_convnext_base.pth is
#     334 MB, so a push containing it does not degrade gracefully — it is
#     refused outright. Tracking these needs Git LFS. Re-pull instead:
#       kaggle kernels output farhantahsinkhan/<slug> -p Kernels/<run>/outputs
#
#   */outputs/saliency/
#     Raw per-image saliency arrays (one .npy per image per method). Fully
#     regenerable, and nothing reads them from git — v16-compare mounts the XAI
#     kernel outputs directly on Kaggle via kernel_sources. Would reach ~156 MB
#     by the end of Phase 3 in exchange for nothing.
*.pth
*/outputs/saliency/

.ipynb_checkpoints/
